g(self):\n        return self.content[self.start : self.end + 1]\n```\n\nYes, I believe that's right.\n\nSo for the key token: content=\"key: value\", start=0, end=2 \u2192 to_string() = \"key\". Good.\n\nSimpler assertions: \n```python\ntoken = tokenize_yaml(b\"key: value\")\nassert isinstance(token, DictToken)\nassert token.start == 0\nassert token.end == 9\nassert token.content == \"key: value\"\nkey_token = list(token.value.keys())[0]\nvalue_token = token.value[key_token]\nassert key_token.to_string() == \"key\"\nassert value_token.to_string() == \"value\"\n```\n\nHmm, but `token.value` \u2014 Token has `value` attribute set in `__init__`? Let me check Token:\n\n```python\nclass Token:\n    def __init__(self, value, start_index, end_index, content=None):\n        self.value = value\n        self.start = start_index\n        self.end = end_index\n        self.content = content if content is not None else \"\"\n```\n\nHmm, I think Token stores `self.value = value`. And there's `get_value()`? Let me check with get_info.\n\nActually from typesystem/tokenize/tokens.py:\n\n```python\nclass Token:\n    def __init__(self, value, start_index, end_index, content=None):\n        self.value = value\n        self.start_index = start_index\n        self.end_index = end_index\n        self.content = content\n\n    def _get_value(self):\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm. I really need to check. Let me use get_info on Token, ScalarToken, DictToken, ListToken.\n\nFrom memory of the typesystem source (version 0.2.x / 3.x):\n\n```python\n# typesystem/tokenize/tokens.py\nfrom typesystem.base import Position\n\n\nclass Token:\n    def __init__(self, value, start_index, end_index, content=None):\n        self.value = value\n        self.start_index = start_index\n        self.end_index = end_index\n        self.content = content\n\n    def _get_value(self):\n        if isinstance(self.value, dict):\n            return {\n                key if isinstance(key, str) else key.to_string(): value\n