e parser expects a document start... Actually the parser would try to parse the flow mapping and fail with \"expected ',' or '}', but got...\" no wait, there's nothing after.\n\nLet me just use a commonly failing example: `\"key: value\\ninvalid\"` \u2014 hmm, that's actually valid? No: `key: value\\ninvalid` \u2014 \"invalid\" at the same indentation level as \"key\" without a colon... that would be a scanner/parser error: \"could not find expected ':'\". Yes, that raises ParserError with problem \"could not find expected ':'\".\n\nActually, let me use something simpler and more reliably an error: `\"{a: b\"` \u2014 unclosed flow mapping \u2192 ParserError \"expected ',' or '}', but got '<stream end>'\"? Hmm, or ScannerError.\n\nOr use a tab: `\"\\ta: b\"` \u2192 ScannerError \"found character '\\\\t' that cannot start any token\". That's reliable.\n\nActually, in YAML, tabs cannot be used for indentation. `yaml.load(\"\\ta: b\")` raises:\n```\nyaml.scanner.ScannerError: found character '\\t' that cannot start any token\n```\nYes, that's reliable.\n\nBut wait \u2014 `\"\\ta: b\".strip()` is `\"a: b\"` which is non-empty, so it passes the empty check. Good.\n\nHmm, but actually let me double check: `\"\\ta: b\"` \u2014 the scanner sees `\\t` at the start... Actually the scanner skips whitespace including tabs? Let me think. In YAML, tabs are allowed as separation space but not indentation. The scanner's `scan_to_next_token` skips spaces and tabs... Hmm, actually:\n\n```python\ndef scan_to_next_token(self):\n    ...\n    while self.peek() == ' ' or self.peek() == '\\t':\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm, actually in newer versions of PyYAML, `scan_to_next_token` skips spaces and tabs when not at the beginning of a line? Let me recall:\n\n```python\ndef scan_to_next_token(self):\n    # Scan until we arrive at '#', at line-break.\n    #\n    # We ignore tabs at the beginning of the line...\n    if self.flow_level == 0 and self.column == 0:\n        found_comment = False\n      